course: dictionary
lesson: 1299
title: Bystander
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bystander is a person who is near when something happens, such as an accident, a fight or bullying, but is not part of it. The clue is in the word: «by» means near, as in «a house by the river». A bystander is close by, but not in the middle of it.
explain: «A bystander is someone who sees something happening to other people.» Ask yourself: is this person near, watching, and not part of it? Then swap in your meaning. "A person near the event who is not part of it" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Bystanders have a choice. «Bystanders can help stop bullying by not joining in, supporting the victim and telling an adult.» A bystander who helps is sometimes called an upstander. Doing nothing can feel like being part of the problem, so think about what you would do.
fact: A bystander is a person who is near when something happens but is not part of it.
fact: «Bystanders» are the people who see bullying happen.
fact: A bystander who joins in or laughs can make bullying worse, so not joining in is a first step.
fact: An «upstander» is a bystander who chooses to help, by telling an adult, comforting the person or getting help.
fact: In an emergency, a bystander can call an ambulance and help until help arrives.
exercise: A bystander is a person who is near when something happens but is not part of it. What is a bystander? | A person who starts a fight | *A person who sees something happen without being part of it | A person who runs very fast | A teacher who runs the school
exercise: «When a fight starts, the most helpful thing a bystander can do is get an adult, not watch or cheer.» What is the most helpful thing a bystander can do? | Film it and laugh | Cheer loudly for one side | *Get an adult | Join in with the fight
exercise: In «Bystanders can help stop bullying by not joining in, supporting the victim and telling an adult», who is the victim? | *The person being bullied | The bystander | The bully | The adult
test: What is one way a bystander can help someone being bullied? | Film it to make fun of them | Join in with the bully | *Tell an adult | Laugh along with the group
test: In first aid, what can a bystander do after an accident? | Take a photo for social media and move on | Argue with the people who were hurt | *Call an ambulance and help until help arrives | Leave the scene straight away
exam: What is an upstander? | A bully who stands up in class | *A bystander who chooses to help | A person who was hurt in an accident | Someone who joins in with bullying
